Input Meaning <code>upload_id</code> Destination staging upload; separate from the uploads selected by the query <code>search_settings.owner</code> <code>visible</code> (default), <code>public</code>, <code>user</code>, <code>shared</code>, or <code>staging</code> <code>search_settings.max_entries</code> Positive limit, bounded by the deployment cap; default is at most 1,000 <code>search_settings.query</code> Search query as JSON text; selects entries <code>search_settings.required</code> Include or exclude directives with <code>type</code> and <code>path</code>; includes also accept <code>resolve_references</code>. Selects archive content <code>export_settings.file_format</code> <code>parquet</code> (default), <code>csv</code>, or <code>json</code> <code>export_settings.create_zip_archive</code> <code>true</code> (default) for ZIP; <code>false</code> for an upload subdirectory <p>For example, this action input selects up to 100 public entries with <code>entry_type</code> equal to <code>ELNSample</code>, then exports their <code>results.method</code> sections as Parquet:</p> <pre><code>{
  "upload_id": "YOUR_STAGING_UPLOAD_ID",
  "search_settings": {
    "owner": "public",
    "max_entries": 100,
    "query": "{\"entry_type\": \"ELNSample\"}",
    "required": [
      {
        "type": "include",
        "path": "results.method",
        "resolve_references": false
      }
    ]
  },
  "export_settings": {
    "file_format": "parquet",
    "create_zip_archive": true
  }
}
</code></pre> <p>Replace the query and paths with ones appropriate to your entries. An include path does not require the entry to contain that path; search filters and archive-content selection have different roles. To follow references beneath an included path, set its <code>resolve_references</code> to <code>true</code>.</p> <p>To export complete archives except for selected paths, use only exclude directives. For example, replace <code>search_settings.required</code> with this list to omit the <code>run</code> section:</p> <pre><code>[
  {
    "type": "exclude",
    "path": "run"
  }
]
</code></pre> <p>Exclude directives do not have a <code>resolve_references</code> option.</p> <p>For REST, wrap this input in <code>{"data": input_json}</code> as shown in the tutorial. Omit <code>user_id</code>; NOMAD supplies the authenticated user's ID.</p>
